          "path": "_m/u/1/0/t/southend-pier-wp/end-of-the-pier-geograph-org-u.jpg",
          "filename": "End Of The Pier - geograph.org.uk - 41364.jpg",
          "caption": "End Of  The Pier. This photo was taken 1 &amp; 1/3rd miles from the shore at the furthest end of the Sun Deck! on the Prince George extension of Southend Pier. The shot was taken looking back towards the RNLI station and lookout post. The RNLI have two inflatable inshore boats on the pier a D- Type and an Atlantic 21. This part of the pier was destroyed after collision with a freighter Kingsashley in 1986 the new RNLI station was opened by the Princess Royal in 1991. For the record it really was that dark and damp!",
          "alt": "End Of  The Pier. This photo was taken 1 &amp; 1/3rd miles from the shore at the furthest end of the Sun Deck! on the Prince George extension of Southend Pier. The shot was taken looking back towards the RNLI station and lookout post. The RNLI have two inflatable inshore boats on the pier a D- Type and an Atlantic 21. This part of the pier was destroyed after collision with a freighter Kingsashley in 1986 the new RNLI station was opened by the Princess Royal in 1991. For the record it really was that dark and damp!",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 482,
